From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jens Willmer <info@jwillmer.de>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 16:15:29 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 105/111] A drag held at the end of the preview selects to the
 last block

At the end of the document, with the pointer in the bottom edge zone or
below the preview, the selection stopped at the last block the pointer
had crossed: a table or code block scrolled sideways did not see a
pointer outside it. When the preview cannot scroll further, the
selection now takes everything to the end of the document (or the start,
at the top), whatever the last block is, until the pointer leaves the
edge; and runs in sideways-scrolled blocks see a drag that passes them.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

